  "summary": "The released 1.1.0 portable scheduler includes station-loss contingency comparisons: inspect retained, removed and replacement contacts, per-request service changes and utility loss, then download complete planning evidence.",
  "rationale": "The existing exact finite-candidate solver and independent exhaustive oracle are preserved. The extracted application proves the hand-checkable 60 + 60 versus 100 greedy trap, a fully lost station and feasible empty service before comparing the actual UI download with its API result. Source-bound native packaging carries the practical replanning workflow into downloads.",
  "limitations": [
    "Invented finite candidates and units; no real radio, ground-station dispatch or operational availability guarantee.",
    "Replanning optimizes the existing objective; it does not guarantee minimum changes to a previous plan.",
    "Unsigned desktop portable folders, not system installers or clean-machine proof. Three-OS extracted-native checks drive an owned URL; default OS browser opening remains manual."
  ],
